WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:04.390
Go! Panther Dancer attacks Puzzle!

00:00:05.990 --> 00:00:07.390
Die!

00:00:07.870 --> 00:00:08.890
I activate my trap!

00:00:09.730 --> 00:00:10.870
Re-dyce-cle!

00:00:11.920 --> 00:00:14.970
Please, my dice roll of fate.

00:00:15.360 --> 00:00:16.970
Go!

00:00:20.150 --> 00:00:21.020
What?

00:00:21.020 --> 00:00:25.630
Yes! Red-Eyed Dice's level becomes 3!

00:00:25.630 --> 00:00:27.040
Let's go!

00:00:27.290 --> 00:00:32.060
Level 3 Red-Eyed Dice tunes Level 4 Puzzle!

00:00:34.960 --> 00:00:37.850
Flap your beautiful and heroic wings,

00:00:37.850 --> 00:00:39.960
to strike the enemy at the speed of light.

00:00:42.960 --> 00:00:44.460
Synchro Summon!

00:00:45.050 --> 00:00:49.590
Appear, Level 7 Clear Wing Synchro Dragon!

00:01:09.960 --> 00:01:12.040
Clear Wing Synchro Dragon...

00:01:16.040 --> 00:01:17.070
Serena!

00:01:18.690 --> 00:01:19.960
Let's go!

00:01:26.130 --> 00:01:29.560
The fun is only getting started!

00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:34.570
D-Wheels.

00:01:35.190 --> 00:01:38.760
Riding duels are fought while 
racing on these machines,

00:01:38.760 --> 00:01:40.460
which are an evolution of the duel disks.

00:01:40.460 --> 00:01:43.900
They combine speed and thrills for the ultimate show,

00:01:43.900 --> 00:01:46.070
a symbol of freedom to all.

00:03:20.150 --> 00:03:24.980
Wings of Crystal

00:03:36.220 --> 00:03:40.430
Serena's Panther Dancer attacked Puzzle.

00:03:40.430 --> 00:03:44.560
Hugo missed the Action Card, so we 
thought he might be out of options,

00:03:44.560 --> 00:03:45.400
but just then...

00:03:45.710 --> 00:03:48.460
He used trap card Re-dyce-cle's effect

00:03:48.460 --> 00:03:52.500
and summoned Clear Wing 
Synchro Dragon to the field!

00:03:54.880 --> 00:03:58.370
I feel like I'm riding on all cylinders right now.

00:03:58.370 --> 00:04:00.190
Right, Rin? Don't you agree?

00:04:00.810 --> 00:04:02.650
I'm not Rin...

00:04:02.650 --> 00:04:04.080
Oh, sorry.

00:04:04.080 --> 00:04:05.160
I thought I told you.

00:04:05.160 --> 00:04:09.000
Changing from the 1300-attack-point Puzzle

00:04:09.000 --> 00:04:13.640
to the 2500-point-Clear Wing 
might reduce damage,

00:04:13.640 --> 00:04:16.840
but it doesn't change your disadvantage.

00:04:17.280 --> 00:04:19.400
Go, Panther Dancer!

00:04:19.400 --> 00:04:21.400
Attack Clear Wing!

00:04:22.080 --> 00:04:25.290
I told you, too. I don't like to give up.

00:04:25.290 --> 00:04:28.180
Damage-reduction isn't all I'm doing!

00:04:28.760 --> 00:04:33.270
I activate trap card Dicetadium of Fate, 
targeting Clear Wing!

00:04:34.520 --> 00:04:35.930
I roll a die.

00:04:35.930 --> 00:04:40.550
If it's even, Clear Wing's attack 
points increase by 1000.

00:04:41.030 --> 00:04:43.560
If it's odd, Clear Wing is destroyed.

00:04:43.850 --> 00:04:46.910
Leaving the match to luck, once more?

00:04:46.910 --> 00:04:49.270
I see. You really don't like to give up.

00:04:49.270 --> 00:04:51.420
Matches come down to momentary luck.

00:04:51.420 --> 00:04:53.750
Go, dice roll!

00:04:55.940 --> 00:04:58.440
The die is 6... It's even!

00:04:58.830 --> 00:05:01.450
Clear Wing's attack points increase!

00:05:02.270 --> 00:05:04.620
3500 attack points?

00:05:05.080 --> 00:05:09.640
Hugo's monster has more attack 
points than Serena's monster.

00:05:09.640 --> 00:05:14.030
If the attack goes through, it's Serena 
who will take damage!

00:05:14.940 --> 00:05:18.680
I thought this duel would be one-sided 
in Serena's favor, but...

00:05:18.680 --> 00:05:20.100
Nice work.

00:05:20.100 --> 00:05:23.070
I turned my disadvantage around to my favor!

00:05:25.800 --> 00:05:28.270
There's nothing I can do, like this.

00:05:28.570 --> 00:05:30.960
Serena, you will not lose.

00:05:30.960 --> 00:05:33.100
I shall not allow you to lose!

00:05:34.100 --> 00:05:37.980
Change course point X4 to GG6 again.

00:05:43.090 --> 00:05:44.620
Another course change?

00:05:45.680 --> 00:05:49.360
Serena, continue down the road to victory.

00:05:57.980 --> 00:06:00.940
Serena brilliantly grabs an Action Card!

00:06:00.940 --> 00:06:03.470
Hey, you're lucky...

00:06:03.470 --> 00:06:07.410
You're in trouble, so the course changes, 
and you get an Action Card.

00:06:08.790 --> 00:06:12.440
Oh, I meant... I think that's a good thing.

00:06:12.440 --> 00:06:14.620
I really like it!

00:06:16.020 --> 00:06:19.020
I activate my Action Card Miracle!

00:06:21.200 --> 00:06:25.730
Its effect halves damage to me, and keeps 
Panther Dancer from being destroyed!

00:06:31.650 --> 00:06:32.730
Good.

00:06:33.880 --> 00:06:38.580
When the Battle Phase ends, Clear Wing's 
attack points return to normal.

00:06:40.100 --> 00:06:43.280
Serena's dueling style is very smart.

00:06:43.680 --> 00:06:45.920
You're great, Serena!

00:06:45.920 --> 00:06:47.990
I love you!

00:06:47.990 --> 00:06:52.690
Great work, Serena and Hugo. 
You guys are the best!

00:06:52.690 --> 00:06:54.860
This is hot... It's so hot.

00:06:54.860 --> 00:06:57.900
Keep the hype going, just like this!

00:06:58.760 --> 00:07:01.870
I set one card and end my turn.

00:07:09.230 --> 00:07:13.610
I don't like to admit it, but it seems 
I was saved by luck, just like you.

00:07:13.610 --> 00:07:14.810
Luck?

00:07:14.810 --> 00:07:16.280
Are you sure about that?

00:07:16.600 --> 00:07:17.480
What?

00:07:17.990 --> 00:07:22.690
It wasn't luck that saved you, 
but the course change.

00:07:24.260 --> 00:07:28.660
Well, even if all City wants you to win...

00:07:28.940 --> 00:07:30.400
I will be the winner!

00:07:30.400 --> 00:07:31.700
Let's go!

00:07:31.700 --> 00:07:33.130
My turn!

00:07:33.130 --> 00:07:34.320
Here it is!

00:07:34.640 --> 00:07:38.010
I summon Speedroid Pachingo-Kart!

00:07:41.730 --> 00:07:43.840
When I successfully summon this card,

00:07:43.840 --> 00:07:47.710
its effect destroys one monster on the field.

00:07:47.960 --> 00:07:52.450
And on the turn I use this effect, 
Pachingo-Kart can't attack.

00:07:53.840 --> 00:07:55.890
I destroy Panther Dancer!

00:07:55.890 --> 00:08:01.090
Sorry, but Panther Dancer cannot be 
destroyed by your card effects.

00:08:03.360 --> 00:08:07.300
Before you negate the destruction effect, 
there's something I should do.

00:08:07.300 --> 00:08:08.030
What?

00:08:08.390 --> 00:08:10.900
I activate Clear Wing's effect.

00:08:16.100 --> 00:08:20.090
When a monster on the field, Level 5 
or above, is targeted by an effect,

00:08:20.940 --> 00:08:25.270
I negate that effect and destroy 
the monster that activated it!

00:08:26.150 --> 00:08:28.200
Dichroic Mirror!

00:08:29.020 --> 00:08:30.590
I choose to destroy

00:08:31.030 --> 00:08:32.540
Pachingo-Kart!

00:08:33.730 --> 00:08:36.520
Thus, until the end of my turn,

00:08:36.520 --> 00:08:42.140
Clear Wing's attack points are increased 
by those of Pachingo-Kart, 1800.

00:08:42.570 --> 00:08:44.940
4300 attack points?

00:08:45.580 --> 00:08:48.160
He wasn't counting on the effect going through.

00:08:48.160 --> 00:08:51.540
He just wanted to increase 
Clear Wing's attack points?

00:08:51.540 --> 00:08:52.510
Let's go!

00:08:52.510 --> 00:08:53.750
Battle!

00:08:53.750 --> 00:08:57.220
I attack Panther Dancer with Clear Wing!

00:09:00.360 --> 00:09:04.420
Change course point XG2 to YZ2.

00:09:07.660 --> 00:09:09.600
There it goes again?

00:09:09.600 --> 00:09:11.130
I didn't ask for this.

00:09:13.830 --> 00:09:17.070
Now, seize the road to victory.

00:09:17.480 --> 00:09:20.540
And the card that will carry me to my dream.

00:09:32.040 --> 00:09:37.220
Serena took the damage, and she 
ignored the Action Card...

00:09:37.220 --> 00:09:39.690
Why? Why did Serena do it?!

00:09:39.690 --> 00:09:42.430
Fool... What is she thinking?

00:09:44.490 --> 00:09:47.760
I don't need anyone to 
create chances for me.

00:09:47.760 --> 00:09:50.170
You're wrong, Serena.

00:09:50.490 --> 00:09:53.570
No matter what happens... 
No matter the situation...

00:09:53.880 --> 00:09:56.270
If you see a chance, take it!

00:09:56.700 --> 00:10:00.810
My childhood friend, who looks like you, 
used to get mad and say that.

00:10:01.220 --> 00:10:02.510
An Action Card?

00:10:02.510 --> 00:10:05.480
That's right, the one you ignored.

00:10:05.790 --> 00:10:07.590
I took it, happily!

00:10:08.570 --> 00:10:12.490
I told you... A duel that relies 
on luck is merely a game.

00:10:13.000 --> 00:10:15.330
I won't treat a duel as a game.

00:10:15.330 --> 00:10:17.960
I'm going to beat you in my own way!

00:10:18.240 --> 00:10:21.060
Dueling my own way, with all I have!

00:10:21.060 --> 00:10:22.650
Sounds great!

00:10:23.700 --> 00:10:26.900
I'll win this duel in my way, too!

00:10:26.900 --> 00:10:30.610
Both of them are declaring 
their expectation of victory.

00:10:30.610 --> 00:10:33.310
This is so exciting!

00:10:46.360 --> 00:10:50.030
I activate my trap card Lunalight 
Reincarnation Dance!

00:10:50.400 --> 00:10:54.770
When a Lunalight Fusion Monster on 
my side of the field is destroyed,

00:10:55.050 --> 00:10:58.300
I can add two Lunalight monsters 
from my deck to my hand.

00:10:59.940 --> 00:11:03.410
Pendulum, huh? Looks like 
you prepared for this.

00:11:03.890 --> 00:11:06.380
Yes, I prepared to win.

00:11:08.000 --> 00:11:10.820
I set one card and end my turn.

00:11:11.150 --> 00:11:14.400
At the same time, Clear Wing's 
monster effect ends,

00:11:14.400 --> 00:11:16.290
and its attack points return to normal.

00:11:24.550 --> 00:12:09.940
Serena! Serena! Serena!

00:11:30.170 --> 00:12:09.940
Hugo! Hugo! Hugo!

00:12:09.940 --> 00:12:12.380
Listen to that excitement.

00:12:12.380 --> 00:12:15.450
Let's rile them up even more!

00:12:17.600 --> 00:12:18.650
Fine.

00:12:22.390 --> 00:12:23.740
Why?

00:12:23.740 --> 00:12:26.280
Why do I feel so excited?

00:12:26.660 --> 00:12:28.140
My heart is racing...

00:12:28.610 --> 00:12:29.910
What's going on here?

00:12:36.530 --> 00:12:40.650
Wait a minute. I feel like there's something 
I should say at a time like this.

00:12:40.650 --> 00:12:42.810
Some catchphrase or something...

00:12:44.280 --> 00:12:47.010
Ladies and gentlemen!

00:12:47.310 --> 00:12:48.710
That's it!

00:13:06.460 --> 00:13:09.310
The duel returns to the highway course.

00:13:09.310 --> 00:13:12.440
What will Serena do? How will Hugo fight?!

00:13:12.800 --> 00:13:14.170
My turn.

00:13:14.170 --> 00:13:17.640
I set the Pendulum Scale

00:13:17.640 --> 00:13:22.010
with Scale 1 Lunalight Wolf and 
Scale 5 Lunalight Tiger!

00:13:28.040 --> 00:13:32.300
Now I can summon monsters between 
Levels 2 and 4 simultaneously!

00:13:33.020 --> 00:13:34.760
Pendulum Summon!

00:13:34.760 --> 00:13:37.240
Come out, my monsters!

00:13:39.960 --> 00:13:41.970
Lunalight Black Sheep.

00:13:42.320 --> 00:13:45.440
And Lunalight Purple Butterfly.

00:13:45.810 --> 00:13:49.320
Here it is, a brilliant Pendulum Summon!

00:13:49.320 --> 00:13:52.140
I activate Lunalight Tiger's Pendulum Effect!

00:13:52.140 --> 00:13:56.090
Once per turn, I can Special Summon 
one Lunalight Fusion Monster

00:13:56.090 --> 00:13:58.600
from my graveyard, with its effects negated.

00:13:59.260 --> 00:14:01.510
Come, Panther Dancer!

00:14:03.570 --> 00:14:08.000
Monsters Special Summoned with Lunalight 
Tiger's effect cannot attack,

00:14:08.000 --> 00:14:10.390
and are destroyed during that turn's End Phase.

00:14:10.660 --> 00:14:14.750
A monster that can't attack, and it's 
destroyed at your End Phase?

00:14:14.750 --> 00:14:17.100
Well, what will you show me next?

00:14:17.440 --> 00:14:20.840
Then, I activate Lunalight Wolf's Pendulum Effect!

00:14:21.150 --> 00:14:25.000
Once per turn, I can perform 
a Fusion Summon with one

00:14:25.000 --> 00:14:27.030
Lunalight Fusion Monster in my Extra Deck.

00:14:28.140 --> 00:14:31.420
Monsters used as fusion 
components by this effect

00:14:31.420 --> 00:14:33.280
are banished, not sent to the graveyard.

00:14:33.730 --> 00:14:38.260
I fuse Panther Dancer, Black Sheep, 
and Purple Butterfly!

00:14:38.720 --> 00:14:42.120
The graceful beast who dances in moonlit fields!

00:14:42.120 --> 00:14:44.350
The beast that hides in the ebony black!

00:14:44.350 --> 00:14:46.470
The butterfly with purple poison!

00:14:46.470 --> 00:14:50.740
Swirl in the moon's gravity and 
be reborn with new power!

00:14:51.180 --> 00:14:52.470
Fusion Summon!

00:14:52.840 --> 00:14:58.170
Appear, king of beasts that dances 
above all, in the moonlight fields!

00:14:58.170 --> 00:15:00.740
Lunalight Leo Dancer!

00:15:02.210 --> 00:15:06.180
Serena summons a monster 
with 3500 attack points!

00:15:06.180 --> 00:15:07.500
Wow...

00:15:07.500 --> 00:15:08.650
Battle!

00:15:08.650 --> 00:15:13.120
Lunalight Leo Dancer attacks 
Clear Wing Synchro Dragon!

00:15:14.650 --> 00:15:15.830
I activate my Action Spell!

00:15:15.830 --> 00:15:18.070
Rejuvenation!

00:15:19.720 --> 00:15:22.370
He used the Action Card I ignored?

00:15:22.680 --> 00:15:27.740
This card's effect increases Clear 
Wing's attack points by 800!

00:15:28.920 --> 00:15:33.000
And Clear Wing isn't destroyed by this battle!

00:15:35.120 --> 00:15:37.240
If I'd gotten that card before,

00:15:37.240 --> 00:15:40.950
I could have prevented Panther Dancer's 
destruction and reduced damage taken.

00:15:40.950 --> 00:15:42.480
That's right.

00:15:42.480 --> 00:15:44.520
But because of that, I can enjoy this duel.

00:15:45.410 --> 00:15:48.230
Wait... I'm enjoying a duel?

00:15:51.130 --> 00:15:54.600
Rejuvenation's effect keeps Clear 
Wing from being destroyed!

00:15:54.890 --> 00:15:56.800
But you do take damage.

00:16:00.000 --> 00:16:02.210
Now, Rejuvenation's effect ends.

00:16:02.560 --> 00:16:05.220
Clear Wing's attack points return to normal.

00:16:07.680 --> 00:16:11.650
Leo Dancer can attack twice 
during a single Battle Phase.

00:16:11.970 --> 00:16:16.620
And after the first attack, I destroy all 
monsters on your side of the field!

00:16:16.620 --> 00:16:18.220
Seriously?

00:16:18.220 --> 00:16:21.590
It seems I still have the advantage...

00:16:21.590 --> 00:16:23.830
You don't know that just yet!

00:16:23.830 --> 00:16:29.300
I do! Leo Dancer's effect destroys 
Clear Wing Synchro Dragon!

00:16:32.410 --> 00:16:34.370
I activate Clear Wing's effect!

00:16:34.720 --> 00:16:37.610
When a monster, Level 5 or above, 
activates an effect,

00:16:37.610 --> 00:16:40.340
I can negate the effect and destroy that monster!

00:16:40.340 --> 00:16:42.640
Dichroic Mirror!

00:16:43.920 --> 00:16:48.290
Leo Dancer cannot be targeted or 
affected by your card's effects.

00:16:48.600 --> 00:16:51.260
Thus, Clear Wing cannot avoid destruction.

00:16:52.620 --> 00:16:54.170
It's not over yet!

00:16:54.170 --> 00:16:56.570
I banish Rejuvenation,

00:16:56.570 --> 00:17:00.100
to activate my Counter Trap Miracle Mirror!

00:17:01.810 --> 00:17:06.300
This turn, Clear Wing cannot be 
destroyed by battle or effects!

00:17:06.620 --> 00:17:11.200
Even if I can't destroy it, Leo Dancer 
still has an attack remaining.

00:17:11.200 --> 00:17:13.080
And you'll take damage from that.

00:17:13.080 --> 00:17:15.050
Go, Leo Dancer!

00:17:18.720 --> 00:17:21.630
Hugo has 200 life points remaining!

00:17:21.630 --> 00:17:23.450
You will not win.

00:17:27.290 --> 00:17:31.130
I see. So you aren't just leaving 
everything to luck, it seems.

00:17:31.700 --> 00:17:33.260
Not bad at all.

00:17:35.880 --> 00:17:37.970
I now end my turn.

00:17:37.970 --> 00:17:41.670
It's a real back-and-forth, 
each shaving off the other's life!

00:17:41.980 --> 00:17:45.180
Truly an appropriate duel for the 
second round's last match.

00:17:45.180 --> 00:17:46.910
Go, Serena!

00:17:46.910 --> 00:17:49.220
Go, Hugo!

00:17:49.220 --> 00:17:52.720
Serena! Serena! Serena!

00:17:52.720 --> 00:17:53.920
The fun...

00:17:53.920 --> 00:17:55.620
...is only getting started!

00:17:57.870 --> 00:17:59.290
My turn!

00:17:59.760 --> 00:18:03.990
I activate the effect of Speedroid Den-Den 
Daiko Duke in my graveyard!

00:18:03.990 --> 00:18:08.170
When my life is below 1000, I can banish it,

00:18:08.170 --> 00:18:11.720
to Special Summon one Tuner 
Monster from my graveyard!

00:18:11.720 --> 00:18:14.790
Come out, Speedroid Red-Eyed Dice.

00:18:24.250 --> 00:18:29.420
Level 1 Red-Eyed Dice tunes 
Level 7 Clear Wing!

00:18:32.160 --> 00:18:35.340
Flap your beautiful and heroic wings,

00:18:35.340 --> 00:18:37.430
to strike the enemy at the speed of light!

00:18:39.860 --> 00:18:41.330
Synchro Summon!

00:18:42.010 --> 00:18:45.700
Appear, Crystal Wing Synchro Dragon!

00:18:48.400 --> 00:18:49.410
Battle!

00:18:50.060 --> 00:18:53.590
You intend to attack Leo Dancer, 
whose attack points are higher?

00:18:53.860 --> 00:18:55.580
Yeah, that's right.

00:18:55.580 --> 00:18:59.780
I attack Leo Dancer with Crystal 
Wing Synchro Dragon!

00:19:01.880 --> 00:19:04.220
Crystal Wing's effect activates.

00:19:04.220 --> 00:19:06.960
When it attacks a monster, Level 5 or above,

00:19:06.960 --> 00:19:10.430
it adds that monster's attack points 
to its own during battle!

00:19:10.430 --> 00:19:13.400
6500 attack points?

00:19:13.400 --> 00:19:15.030
Now, it's over!

00:19:15.600 --> 00:19:18.860
Gale Crystallos Edge!

00:19:37.020 --> 00:19:41.720
F-Finally, an end to that 
incredible back-and-forth.

00:19:42.230 --> 00:19:45.430
The winner is Hugo!

00:19:45.430 --> 00:19:49.150
Both did absolutely everything they 
could. What a magnificent duel.

00:19:49.150 --> 00:19:51.340
Let's have applause for the loser, Serena.

00:20:12.980 --> 00:20:14.160
That was fun...

00:20:15.430 --> 00:20:18.850
I never knew a duel could be so fun.

00:20:18.850 --> 00:20:19.960
Thank you.

00:20:19.960 --> 00:20:23.130
I don't know how to react to 
thanks from the one I beat.

00:20:26.690 --> 00:20:27.590
Yuya?

00:20:28.960 --> 00:20:30.740
Oh, nothing.

00:20:30.740 --> 00:20:31.690
Hugo...

00:20:31.690 --> 00:20:32.470
What?

00:20:42.690 --> 00:20:44.390
I'll root for you to win.

00:20:44.700 --> 00:20:46.010
O-Okay.

00:20:46.860 --> 00:20:48.540
Look at this.

00:20:48.540 --> 00:20:52.440
A firm handshake between two 
duelists who've given it their all.

00:20:52.440 --> 00:20:56.250
This is how the Friendship Cup should be!

00:20:59.460 --> 00:21:01.740
R-R-Rin...

00:21:06.370 --> 00:21:07.410
R-Rin!

00:21:12.880 --> 00:21:15.550
Hey, things were going well for a minute.

00:21:17.360 --> 00:21:21.370
Y-You didn't have to hit me that hard...

00:21:24.050 --> 00:21:26.460
Make everyone smile with your duel, eh?

00:21:27.360 --> 00:21:30.400
Yuya, I think I finally understand

00:21:30.400 --> 00:21:32.830
what you were talking about, a bit.

00:21:38.870 --> 00:21:40.600
H-Huh?

00:21:44.390 --> 00:21:46.660
Was I dueling?

00:21:48.370 --> 00:21:50.940
Rooting for me to win, huh?

00:21:52.390 --> 00:21:54.030
Okay, I'm gonna do it—

00:23:49.890 --> 00:23:53.430
